204	
205	## Available Servers
206	
207	### Core Servers
208	
209	| Server | Description | Directory |
210	|--------|-------------|-----------|
211	| **Qiskit MCP Server** | Circuit creation, transpilation, and serialization (QASM3, QPY) using [Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit) | [`qiskit-mcp-server/`](./qiskit-mcp-server/) |
212	| **Qiskit Code Assistant** | AI-assisted quantum programming via [IBM Qiskit Code Assistant](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/qiskit-code-assistant) | [`qiskit-code-assistant-mcp-server/`](./qiskit-code-assistant-mcp-server/) |
213	| **Qiskit IBM Runtime** | Full access to IBM Quantum hardware via [Qiskit IBM Runtime](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime/) | [`qiskit-ibm-runtime-mcp-server/`](./qiskit-ibm-runtime-mcp-server/) |
214	| **Qiskit IBM Transpiler** | AI-optimized circuit routing and optimization via [qiskit-ibm-transpiler](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-transpiler) | [`qiskit-ibm-transpiler-mcp-server/`](./qiskit-ibm-transpiler-mcp-server/) |
215	| **Qiskit Docs** | Search and retrieve [Qiskit documentation](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/), guides, and API references. No auth required. | [`qiskit-docs-mcp-server/`](./qiskit-docs-mcp-server/) |
216	
217	### Community Servers
218	
219	| Server | Description | Directory |
220	|--------|-------------|-----------|
221	| **Qiskit Gym** | RL-based quantum circuit synthesis using [qiskit-gym](https://github.com/rl-institut/qiskit-gym) (permutation routing, linear functions, Clifford circuits) | [`qiskit-gym-mcp-server/`](./qiskit-gym-mcp-server/) |
222	
223	## Examples
224	
225	Each server includes an `examples/` directory with a **Jupyter notebook** (`langchain_agent.ipynb`) and a **Python script** (`langchain_agent.py`) showing how to build AI agents with LangChain.
226	
227	The root [`examples/`](./examples/) directory contains a multi-agent **Quantum Volume Finder** that orchestrates multiple MCP servers to find the highest achievable Quantum Volume on IBM Quantum hardware. See the [examples README](./examples/README.md) for details.
228	
229	## Architecture
230	
231	All servers are built on [FastMCP](https://github.com/jlowin/fastmcp) and share a consistent structure:
232	
233	- **Async-first** — all tool and resource handlers are async, using FastMCP's native async support
234	- **Standalone packages** — each server is an independent PyPI package with its own `pyproject.toml`, tests, and CI
235	- **MCP Registry** — every server ships a [`server.json`](https://registry.modelcontextprotocol.io/) manifest for automatic discovery
236	- **Unified meta-package** — `qiskit-mcp-servers` installs any combination via pip extras
237	- **Full MCP protocol** — tools (quantum operations), resources (backend info, service status), and stdio transport
238	
239	## Development
240	
241	### Running Tests
242	```bash
243	cd qiskit-code-assistant-mcp-server  # or any server directory
244	./run_tests.sh
245	```
246	
247	### Code Quality
248	- **Linting**: `ruff check` and `ruff format`
249	- **Type checking**: `mypy src/`
250	- **Testing**: `pytest` with async support and coverage reporting
251	- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions for automated testing
