15	
16	A collection of [Model Context Protocol (MCP)](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/introduction) servers that give AI assistants, LLMs, and agents seamless access to IBM Quantum services and Qiskit libraries. Generate quantum code, connect to real hardware, analyze backends, execute circuits, and search Qiskit documentation — all through a standardized protocol that works with any MCP-compatible client.
17	
18	## Quick Start
19	
20	### Prerequisites
21	
22	- **Python 3.10+** (3.11+ recommended)
23	- **IBM Quantum account** and [API token](https://quantum.ibm.com) (only required for IBM cloud servers: Runtime, Transpiler, Code Assistant)
24	
25	### Install from PyPI
26	
27	```bash
28	# Install all servers (core + community)
29	pip install "qiskit-mcp-servers[all]"
30	
31	# Install core servers only (default, excludes community)
32	pip install qiskit-mcp-servers
33	```
34	
35	<details>
36	<summary>Install individual servers</summary>
37	
38	```bash
39	pip install "qiskit-mcp-servers[qiskit]"          # Qiskit server only
40	pip install "qiskit-mcp-servers[code-assistant]"  # Code Assistant server only
41	pip install "qiskit-mcp-servers[runtime]"         # IBM Runtime server only
42	pip install "qiskit-mcp-servers[transpiler]"      # IBM Transpiler server only
43	pip install "qiskit-mcp-servers[docs]"            # Documentation server only
44	pip install "qiskit-mcp-servers[gym]"             # Qiskit Gym server only (community)
45	```
46	
47	</details>
48	
49	### Install from Source
50	
51	Each server runs independently — the directory name and command are the same:
52	
53	```bash
54	cd qiskit-mcp-server  # or any server directory
55	pip install -e .
56	qiskit-mcp-server
57	```
58	
59	### Configuration
60	
61	Servers that connect to IBM Quantum cloud services require a `QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN` environment variable. See each server's README for the full list of environment variables and configuration options.
62	
63	```bash
64	export QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN="your_ibm_quantum_token_here"
65	```
66	
67	### Client Setup
68	
69	All servers are compatible with any MCP client. Pick your client below.
70	
71	#### Claude Code
72	
73	[![Claude Code Video](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/161797b0-59d9-4632-bafa-12d50bfef226)](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/161797b0-59d9-4632-bafa-12d50bfef226)
74	
75	```bash
76	# No auth required
77	claude mcp add qiskit -- uvx qiskit-mcp-server
78	claude mcp add qiskit-docs -- uvx qiskit-docs-mcp-server
79	claude mcp add qiskit-gym -- uvx qiskit-gym-mcp-server
80	
81	# Require QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN (https://quantum.ibm.com)
82	claude mcp add qiskit-code-assistant -e QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN=$QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN -- uvx qiskit-code-assistant-mcp-server
83	claude mcp add qiskit-ibm-runtime -e QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN=$QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN -- uvx qiskit-ibm-runtime-mcp-server
84	claude mcp add qiskit-ibm-transpiler -e QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN=$QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN -- uvx qiskit-ibm-transpiler-mcp-server
85	```
86	
